WEBVTT

00:03:26.953 --> 00:03:30.414
But if used smartly,
it's just an amazing thing.

00:03:31.582 --> 00:03:35.544
Biochar is carbon
resulting from pyrolysis,

00:03:35.586 --> 00:03:40.216
that is, heating biomass
at high temperature without oxygen.

00:03:41.092 --> 00:03:44.220
Any kind of plant-based, dried biomass

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:47.598
contains about half of its weight
in the form of carbon.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:51.519
And it is this carbon
that is extracted and stabilized

00:03:51.519 --> 00:03:52.728
to create biochar.

00:03:53.562 --> 00:03:55.731
Biochar is essentially carbon

00:03:55.773 --> 00:03:58.150
that was captured
from the atmosphere by plants

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:01.070
and transformed
into a very stable form of carbon.